# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS TO OVERRIDE .gitignore. When .gcloudignore is absent, gcloud
# generates one from .gitignore — which excludes chroma_db/, because a 553MB
# derived artifact has no business in git. The result is a deploy that succeeds,
# a service that starts cleanly, and every single search returning nothing,
# because the image shipped without an index. Silent and confusing.
#
# So chroma_db/ is deliberately NOT listed below. It has to reach the builder.
# See the CHROMA_DIR note in the Dockerfile for why it lives in the image.

# The Windows virtualenv: 6.1GB, and useless in a Linux image anyway — the
# Dockerfile installs Linux wheels from requirements.txt.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# 71MB of concatenated Yelp reviews, input to the one-time seed scripts only.
tagged_reviews.txt
data/
*.parquet
*.csv

# Notebooks and the stray Node install.
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
node_modules/
package-lock.json
package.json

# Secrets come from Cloud Run's environment, never from an uploaded file.
# env.yaml is the local file passed to --env-vars-file: gcloud reads it on THIS
# machine and sends the values over the API, so it must never be uploaded into
# the build context or baked into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
env.yaml

# Local noise.
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
